export const CLINICA = {"generato":"2026-11-06","dieta":[{"id":"lupus_alfalfa","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["alfalfa sprouts","alfalfa seeds","alfalfa tablets"],"it":"Evita germogli, semi e compresse di erba medica (alfalfa): contengono L-canavanina, che in studi su primati e in rari casi umani è stata associata a un quadro simile al lupus; la Johns Hopkins Lupus Center consiglia di evitarli completamente.","en":"Avoid alfalfa sprouts, seeds and tablets: they contain L-canavanine, which was linked to a lupus-like syndrome in primate feeding studies and in rare human case reports; the Johns Hopkins Lupus Center advises avoiding them completely.","evidenza":"patient-org-advice","fonti":[{"titolo":"5 Things to Avoid if You Have Lupus (page modified 2019-07-29)","editore":"Johns Hopkins Lupus Center","anno":2019,"url":"https://www.hopkinslupus.org/lupus-info/lifestyle-additional-information/avoid/"},{"titolo":"Systemic lupus erythematosus-like syndrome in monkeys fed alfalfa sprouts: role of a nonprotein amino acid (Malinow MR et al., Science 1982;216:415-417)","editore":"PubMed","anno":1982,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/7071589/"},{"titolo":"Dietary amino acid-induced systemic lupus erythematosus (Montanaro A, Bardana EJ, Rheum Dis Clin North Am 1991;17:323-332)","editore":"PubMed","anno":1991,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1862241/"},{"titolo":"Role of non-protein amino acid L-canavanine in autoimmunity (Akaogi J et al., Autoimmun Rev 2006;5:429-435)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2006,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16890899/"}]},{"id":"lupus_raw_sprouts_immunosuppressed","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["raw or lightly cooked sprouts of any kind (alfalfa, clover, radish, mung bean, onion)"],"it":"Se assumi immunosoppressori: niente germogli crudi o poco cotti di nessun tipo. La FDA indica che le persone con sistema immunitario indebolito sono più vulnerabili alle infezioni alimentari e dovrebbero evitarli.","en":"If you take immunosuppressants: no raw or lightly cooked sprouts of any kind. The FDA states that people with weakened immune systems are more vulnerable to foodborne illness and should avoid them.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"Selecting and Serving Produce Safely (content current as of 03/05/2024)","editore":"U.S. Food and Drug Administration","anno":2024,"url":"https://www.fda.gov/food/buy-store-serve-safe-food/selecting-and-serving-produce-safely"}]},{"id":"lupus_garlic","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["garlic","garlic supplements"],"it":"Aglio: la Johns Hopkins Lupus Center suggerisce di evitarlo in cucina perché allicina, ajoene e tiosulfinati stimolerebbero i globuli bianchi, ma precisa che una piccolissima quantità non fa male. Le prove sono di laboratorio, non studi clinici sul lupus. Gli integratori di aglio vanno discussi con il medico.","en":"Garlic: the Johns Hopkins Lupus Center suggests avoiding cooking with garlic because allicin, ajoene and thiosulfinates may stimulate white blood cells, while stating that a tiny amount will not harm. The evidence is mechanistic, not clinical studies in lupus. Discuss garlic supplements with the doctor.","evidenza":"patient-org-advice","fonti":[{"titolo":"5 Things to Avoid if You Have Lupus (page modified 2019-07-29)","editore":"Johns Hopkins Lupus Center","anno":2019,"url":"https://www.hopkinslupus.org/lupus-info/lifestyle-additional-information/avoid/"},{"titolo":"Identifying immunostimulatory herbal supplements that may flare autoimmune skin diseases: a systematic scoping review (Weiner JD et al., Lupus Sci Med 2025)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41475897/"}]},{"id":"lupus_immunostimulant_supplements","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["echinacea","alfalfa","ashwagandha","astragalus","chlorella","garlic supplements","ginseng","green tea extract","Indian mulberry (noni)","liquorice","mistletoe","reishi mushroom","skullcap","spirulina","tinospora"],"it":"Evita gli integratori 'per le difese immunitarie' senza il consenso del medico. La monografia EMA sull'echinacea ne sconsiglia l'uso in caso di malattie autoimmuni, immunodeficienze e immunosoppressione; una revisione sistematica del 2025 elenca 15 erbe con le prove più solide di effetto immunostimolante (tra cui echinacea, alfalfa, spirulina, clorella, ginseng, astragalo).","en":"Avoid 'immune-boosting' supplements unless the doctor agrees. The EMA echinacea monograph advises against use in autoimmune diseases, immunodeficiencies and immunosuppression; a 2025 systematic scoping review lists 15 herbs with the strongest immunostimulatory evidence (including echinacea, alfalfa, spirulina, chlorella, ginseng and astragalus).","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"European Union herbal monograph on Echinacea purpurea (L.) Moench, herba recens (EMA/HMPC/48704/2014 Corr 1), section 4.4","editore":"European Medicines Agency, Committee on Herbal Medicinal Products","anno":2015,"url":"https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/herbal-monograph/final-european-union-herbal-monograph-echinacea-purpurea-l-moench-herba-recens_en.pdf"},{"titolo":"Identifying immunostimulatory herbal supplements that may flare autoimmune skin diseases: a systematic scoping review (Weiner JD et al., Lupus Sci Med 2025)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41475897/"},{"titolo":"5 Things to Avoid if You Have Lupus (page modified 2019-07-29)","editore":"Johns Hopkins Lupus Center","anno":2019,"url":"https://www.hopkinslupus.org/lupus-info/lifestyle-additional-information/avoid/"}]},{"id":"lupus_omega3","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["omega-3 supplement (fish oil, EPA/DHA)"],"it":"Integratore di omega-3: una meta-analisi di 5 RCT (274 pazienti, dosi fino a 3 g al giorno) ha trovato una piccola riduzione dell'attività del lupus (circa 0,9 punti SLEDAI), con certezza delle prove bassa. Da iniziare solo con il consenso del medico, soprattutto se assumi anticoagulanti o antinfiammatori (FANS): gli omega-3 possono interagire con i farmaci che agiscono sulla coagulazione.","en":"Omega-3 supplement: a meta-analysis of 5 RCTs (274 patients, doses up to 3 g/day) found a small reduction in lupus activity (about 0.9 SLEDAI points), with low-certainty evidence. Start only with the doctor's approval, especially if you take anticoagulants or NSAIDs, because omega-3 supplements may interact with drugs that affect blood clotting.","evidenza":"meta-analysis","fonti":[{"titolo":"Effect of omega-3 fatty acids on systemic lupus erythematosus disease activity: a systematic review and meta-analysis (Duarte-García A et al., Autoimmun Rev 2020;19:102688)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2020,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33131703/"},{"titolo":"Things To Know About Omegas for Heart Disease","editore":"NIH National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH)","anno":null,"url":"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/tips/things-to-know-about-omegas-for-heart-disease"},{"titolo":"Lupus Diet (page modified 2022-07-15)","editore":"Johns Hopkins Lupus Center","anno":2022,"url":"https://www.hopkinslupus.org/lupus-info/lifestyle-additional-information/lupus-diet/"}]},{"id":"lupus_vitamin_d","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"monitor","cibi":["vitamin D supplement"],"it":"Vitamina D: KDIGO 2024 raccomanda calcio e vitamina D per proteggere le ossa nella nefrite lupica ed EULAR raccomanda di verificare l'apporto di calcio e vitamina D in tutti i pazienti con lupus. L'effetto sull'attività del lupus è incerto: le meta-analisi di RCT danno risultati discordanti. Dose e controlli del 25-OH vitamina D li decide il medico.","en":"Vitamin D: KDIGO 2024 recommends calcium and vitamin D for bone protection in lupus nephritis, and EULAR advises checking calcium and vitamin D intake in all people with lupus. The effect on lupus activity is uncertain: meta-analyses of RCTs disagree. Dose and 25-OH vitamin D checks are for the doctor to decide.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Lupus Nephritis (Kidney Int 2024;105(1S):S1-S69)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/KDIGO_2024_Lupus_Nephritis_Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"EULAR recommendations for monitoring patients with systemic lupus erythematosus in clinical practice and in observational studies (Mosca M et al., Ann Rheum Dis 2010;69:1269-1274)","editore":"EULAR / Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases (PMC full text)","anno":2010,"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2952401/"},{"titolo":"Efficacy and Safety of Vitamin D Supplementation in Patients With Systemic Lupus Erythematosus: A Meta-analysis of Randomized Controlled Trials (Zheng R et al., Am J Med Sci 2019;358:104-114)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2019,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31331447/"},{"titolo":"A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis of the Effects of Vitamin D on Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (El Kababi S et al., Nutrients 2025;17:2794)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40944182/"},{"titolo":"Effects of vitamin D supplementation on patients with systemic lupus erythematosus: a systematic review and meta-analysis (Lu J et al., Autoimmun Rev 2026;25:104057)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41951148/"}]},{"id":"ln_sodium","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"limit","cibi":["table salt","high-sodium processed and ultra-processed foods"],"it":"Sale: KDIGO indica sodio inferiore a 2 g al giorno (meno di 90 mmol, cioè meno di 5 g di sale) nelle malattie glomerulari, per controllare pressione, edemi e proteinuria; la linea guida KDIGO 2024 sulla nefrite lupica indica di evitare una dieta ricca di sodio.","en":"Salt: KDIGO advises dietary sodium below 2 g/day (below 90 mmol/day, i.e. below 5 g of salt) in glomerular disease to help control blood pressure, oedema and proteinuria; the KDIGO 2024 lupus nephritis guideline lists avoiding a high-sodium diet.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Lupus Nephritis (Kidney Int 2024;105(1S):S1-S69)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/KDIGO_2024_Lupus_Nephritis_Guideline.pdf"}]},{"id":"ln_blood_pressure","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"monitor","cibi":[],"it":"Pressione arteriosa: KDIGO suggerisce, se tollerata, una pressione sistolica inferiore a 120 mmHg misurata in modo standardizzato in ambulatorio, insieme a meno sale, peso normale, attività fisica regolare e niente fumo.","en":"Blood pressure: KDIGO suggests, when tolerated, a systolic pressure below 120 mmHg using standardised office measurement, together with less salt, normal weight, regular exercise and no smoking.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"}]},{"id":"ln_protein","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"monitor","cibi":["protein foods (fish, poultry, eggs, dairy, legumes)"],"it":"Proteine: con proteinuria (nefrosica nella figura KDIGO) KDIGO 2021 suggerisce da 0,8 a 1,0 g/kg al giorno calcolati sul peso ideale; con eGFR sotto 60 ml/min/1,73 m2 circa 0,8 g/kg al giorno, senza scendere sotto 0,6 g/kg; nella malattia renale cronica a rischio di progressione va evitato più di 1,3 g/kg al giorno. Non abbiamo trovato una restrizione KDIGO per eGFR normale senza proteinuria: il piano attuale (circa 1 g/kg) va rivisto dal nefrologo se cambiano eGFR o proteinuria.","en":"Protein: with proteinuria (nephrotic-range in the KDIGO figure) KDIGO 2021 suggests 0.8 to 1.0 g/kg/day based on ideal body weight; with eGFR below 60 ml/min/1.73 m2 about 0.8 g/kg/day and never below 0.6 g/kg/day; in CKD at risk of progression avoid more than 1.3 g/kg/day. We found no KDIGO protein restriction for normal eGFR without proteinuria: the current plan (about 1 g/kg) should be reviewed by the nephrologist if eGFR or proteinuria change.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"}]},{"id":"ln_potassium_phosphorus","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"monitor","cibi":["processed foods rich in bioavailable potassium","phosphate additives"],"it":"Potassio e fosforo: KDIGO consiglia di limitare i cibi ricchi di potassio biodisponibile (per esempio alimenti trasformati) nella malattia renale cronica da G3 a G5 con precedenti di iperkaliemia o nei periodi a rischio, e di limitare il fosfato alimentare per trattare un fosfato alto nella malattia renale cronica da G3a a G5D. Con funzione renale e valori normali queste linee guida non prevedono restrizioni; il potassio va però ricontrollato quando si iniziano o aumentano ACE-inibitori o sartani, e con inibitori della calcineurina.","en":"Potassium and phosphorus: KDIGO advises limiting foods rich in bioavailable potassium (for example processed foods) in CKD G3 to G5 with a history of hyperkalaemia or during high-risk periods, and limiting dietary phosphate to treat high phosphate in CKD G3a to G5D. With normal kidney function and normal levels these guidelines set no restriction; potassium should be rechecked when ACE inhibitors or ARBs are started or increased, and with calcineurin inhibitors.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2017 Clinical Practice Guideline Update for CKD-Mineral and Bone Disorder (Kidney Int Suppl 2017;7:1-59)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2017,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/2017-KDIGO-CKD-MBD-GL-Update.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"},{"titolo":"LUPKYNIS (voclosporin) capsules, US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 27, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=9f489295-1156-52c7-5fd0-5c4c52f9b813"},{"titolo":"PROGRAF (tacrolimus), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Mar 21, 2025)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7f667de1-9dfa-4bd6-8ba0-15ee2d78873b"}]},{"id":"ln_plant_based","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"prefer","cibi":["vegetables","legumes","fruit","naturally gluten-free whole grains"],"it":"Nella malattia renale cronica KDIGO 2024 consiglia una dieta varia con più alimenti vegetali che animali e meno alimenti ultra-processati; KDIGO 2021 indica di favorire, quando possibile, le proteine vegetali.","en":"In CKD, KDIGO 2024 advises a varied diet with more plant-based than animal-based foods and fewer ultra-processed foods; KDIGO 2021 advises favouring plant protein sources when possible.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"}]},{"id":"ln_weight_activity","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"prefer","cibi":[],"it":"Peso e movimento: KDIGO 2021 indica la riduzione calorica per raggiungere un BMI normale e ridurre il grasso addominale nelle malattie glomerulari; KDIGO 2024 raccomanda nella malattia renale cronica almeno 150 minuti a settimana di attività moderata (il piano prevede 5 volte 30 minuti); EULAR 2023 include esercizio regolare e dieta equilibrata tra le misure non farmacologiche del lupus.","en":"Weight and activity: KDIGO 2021 advises calorie restriction to reach a normal BMI and limit central adiposity in glomerular disease; KDIGO 2024 recommends at least 150 minutes per week of moderate activity in CKD (the plan has 5 x 30 minutes); EULAR 2023 lists regular exercise and a healthy balanced diet among non-drug measures in lupus.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"KDIGO 2021 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Glomerular Diseases (Kidney Int 2021;100(4S):S1-S276)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2021,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/02/KDIGO-Glomerular-Diseases-Guideline-2021-English.pdf"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"EULAR recommendations for the management of systemic lupus erythematosus: 2023 update (Fanouriakis A et al., Ann Rheum Dis 2024;83:15-29); full text read from the Leiden University repository copy https://hdl.handle.net/1887/3750414","editore":"EULAR","anno":2024,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/ard-2023-224762"}]},{"id":"drug_grapefruit_cni","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["grapefruit","grapefruit juice","pomelo","Seville (bitter) orange and its marmalade","tangelo"],"it":"Se assumi ciclosporina, tacrolimus o voclosporina: niente pompelmo né succo di pompelmo (lo indicano le schede tecniche). La FDA avverte che anche pomelo, arancia amara di Siviglia (usata per la marmellata) e tangelo possono avere lo stesso effetto; un caso clinico ha descritto un forte aumento del tacrolimus nel sangue dopo il pomelo.","en":"If you take cyclosporine, tacrolimus or voclosporin: no grapefruit or grapefruit juice (stated in the drug labels). The FDA warns that pomelo, Seville orange (used for marmalade) and tangelo may have the same effect; a case report described a marked rise in blood tacrolimus after pomelo.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"NEORAL (cyclosporine), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 11, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=94461af3-11f1-4670-95d4-2965b9538ae3"},{"titolo":"PROGRAF (tacrolimus), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Mar 21, 2025)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7f667de1-9dfa-4bd6-8ba0-15ee2d78873b"},{"titolo":"LUPKYNIS (voclosporin) capsules, US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 27, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=9f489295-1156-52c7-5fd0-5c4c52f9b813"},{"titolo":"Grapefruit Juice and Some Drugs Don't Mix (content current as of 07/01/2021)","editore":"U.S. Food and Drug Administration","anno":2021,"url":"https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/grapefruit-juice-and-some-drugs-dont-mix"},{"titolo":"Pomelo-induced increase in the blood level of tacrolimus in a renal transplant patient (Egashira K et al., Transplantation 2003;75:1057)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2003,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12698101/"}]},{"id":"drug_st_johns_wort","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["St John's wort (Hypericum) supplements"],"it":"Con ciclosporina evita l'iperico (erba di San Giovanni): la scheda riporta una forte riduzione dei livelli di ciclosporina nel sangue. Con tacrolimus o voclosporina chiedi al medico prima di qualsiasi integratore, perché le schede avvertono sugli induttori del CYP3A4.","en":"With cyclosporine avoid St John's wort: the label reports a marked fall in blood cyclosporine levels. With tacrolimus or voclosporin ask the doctor before any supplement, because their labels warn about CYP3A4 inducers.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"NEORAL (cyclosporine), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 11, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=94461af3-11f1-4670-95d4-2965b9538ae3"},{"titolo":"LUPKYNIS (voclosporin) capsules, US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 27, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=9f489295-1156-52c7-5fd0-5c4c52f9b813"},{"titolo":"PROGRAF (tacrolimus), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Mar 21, 2025)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7f667de1-9dfa-4bd6-8ba0-15ee2d78873b"}]},{"id":"drug_cni_meal_timing","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["meal timing","high-fat meals"],"it":"Voclosporina: a stomaco vuoto, 1 ora prima o 2 ore dopo un pasto, circa ogni 12 ore. Tacrolimus: il cibo, soprattutto un pasto grasso, ne riduce l'assorbimento; se lo prendi con il cibo, fallo sempre allo stesso modo.","en":"Voclosporin: on an empty stomach, 1 hour before or 2 hours after a meal, about every 12 hours. Tacrolimus: food, especially a high-fat meal, reduces absorption; if taken with food, always take it the same way.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"LUPKYNIS (voclosporin) capsules, US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 27, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=9f489295-1156-52c7-5fd0-5c4c52f9b813"},{"titolo":"PROGRAF (tacrolimus), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Mar 21, 2025)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2025,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=7f667de1-9dfa-4bd6-8ba0-15ee2d78873b"}]},{"id":"drug_hcq_food","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["food or milk at dosing","antacids","kaolin"],"it":"Idrossiclorochina: la scheda USA indica di assumerla con cibo o latte. Antiacidi e caolino riducono l'assorbimento della clorochina (intervallo di almeno 4 ore) e per l'idrossiclorochina l'interazione non può essere esclusa.","en":"Hydroxychloroquine: the US label says to take it with food or milk. Antacids and kaolin reduce chloroquine absorption (keep at least 4 hours apart) and an interaction with hydroxychloroquine cannot be ruled out.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"PLAQUENIL (hydroxychloroquine sulfate), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated May 21, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=34496b43-05a2-45fb-a769-52b12e099341"}]},{"id":"drug_mycophenolate_timing","condizione":"lupus_nephritis","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["meal timing","antacids with magnesium or aluminium hydroxide"],"it":"Micofenolato mofetile (CellCept): la scheda raccomanda di assumerlo a stomaco vuoto. Acido micofenolico (Myfortic): 1 ora prima o 2 ore dopo il cibo. Gli antiacidi con idrossido di magnesio o di alluminio ne riducono l'assorbimento: non prenderli insieme (per CellCept l'antiacido almeno 2 ore dopo).","en":"Mycophenolate mofetil (CellCept): the label recommends taking it on an empty stomach. Mycophenolic acid (Myfortic): 1 hour before or 2 hours after food. Antacids with magnesium or aluminium hydroxide reduce absorption: do not take them together (for CellCept the antacid at least 2 hours later).","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"CELLCEPT (mycophenolate mofetil), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 10, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=37241e87-4af4-4dc3-a1aa-ea6f20d8dc40"},{"titolo":"MYFORTIC (mycophenolic acid) delayed-release tablets, US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Aug 11, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=eed26501-890d-4ff6-88e7-6dbea4726e53"}]},{"id":"drug_azathioprine_meals","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["meal timing"],"it":"Azatioprina: secondo la scheda, i disturbi di stomaco spesso si riducono dividendo la dose e/o assumendola dopo i pasti.","en":"Azathioprine: per the label, stomach upset can often be reduced by divided doses and/or taking it after meals.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"IMURAN (azathioprine), US prescribing information (DailyMed version dated Sep 14, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=4d62b6e4-a9d4-4818-e063-6394a90aa208"}]},{"id":"drug_glucocorticoids_salt_sugar_bone","condizione":"lupus","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["salt","sugars and sweets","calcium-rich foods","potassium"],"it":"Cortisonici (per esempio prednisone): la scheda riporta ritenzione di sodio e liquidi, perdita di potassio, aumento dell'escrezione di calcio e ridotta tolleranza al glucosio, e indica che possono servire meno sale e potassio supplementare. KDIGO 2024 raccomanda nella nefrite lupica calcio (apporto ottimale da 1000 a 1200 mg al giorno) e vitamina D; EULAR consiglia controlli della glicemia più frequenti in chi assume cortisonici.","en":"Glucocorticoids (for example prednisone): the label lists sodium and fluid retention, potassium loss, increased calcium excretion and decreased glucose tolerance, and says dietary salt restriction and potassium supplementation may be necessary. KDIGO 2024 recommends calcium (optimal intake 1000 to 1200 mg/day) and vitamin D in lupus nephritis; EULAR advises more frequent glucose checks for people on glucocorticoids.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"Prednisone tablets USP (generic), US label (DailyMed version dated Nov 05, 2026)","editore":"U.S. FDA-approved label via NIH NLM DailyMed","anno":2026,"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=c21be016-6b25-4e09-b253-23b58884ccb6"},{"titolo":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Lupus Nephritis (Kidney Int 2024;105(1S):S1-S69)","editore":"KDIGO","anno":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/KDIGO_2024_Lupus_Nephritis_Guideline.pdf"},{"titolo":"EULAR recommendations for monitoring patients with systemic lupus erythematosus in clinical practice and in observational studies (Mosca M et al., Ann Rheum Dis 2010;69:1269-1274)","editore":"EULAR / Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases (PMC full text)","anno":2010,"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2952401/"}]},{"id":"celiac_strict_gfd","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"avoid","cibi":["wheat","barley","rye","spelt","farro","khorasan (Kamut)","einkorn","triticale","bulgur","seitan","oats not labelled gluten-free"],"it":"Dieta senza glutine rigorosa e per tutta la vita (raccomandazione forte ESsCD): niente frumento, orzo, segale e loro varietà (farro, spelta, Kamut, monococco, triticale, bulgur, seitan) né avena non certificata.","en":"Strict lifelong gluten-free diet (strong ESsCD recommendation): no wheat, barley, rye or their varieties (farro, spelt, Kamut, einkorn, triticale, bulgur, seitan) and no non-certified oats.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD) guideline for coeliac disease and other gluten-related disorders (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2019;7(5):583-613; PMC6545713); full text read from a publisher PDF copy","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2019,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2050640619844125"},{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"},{"titolo":"I cereali vietati (page modified 2026-03-12)","editore":"AIC Associazione Italiana Celiachia","anno":2026,"url":"https://www.celiachia.it/dieta-senza-glutine/gestire-dieta-senza-glutine/i-cereali-vietati/"}]},{"id":"celiac_oats","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["oats","oat flakes","oat bran"],"it":"Avena: solo avena certificata senza glutine (in etichetta 'senza glutine'); l'avena comune è spesso contaminata. ESsCD 2025 la raccomanda già dalla diagnosi (una piccola minoranza può reagire all'avenina) e ACG 2023 la raccomanda con monitoraggio della tolleranza. AIC la ritiene idonea per chi è in remissione clinica e sierologica e ha escluso anche l'avena da almeno sei mesi, iniziando sotto controllo medico.","en":"Oats: only certified gluten-free oats (labelled 'gluten-free'); ordinary oats are often contaminated. ESsCD 2025 recommends them from diagnosis (a small subset may react to avenin) and ACG 2023 recommends them with monitoring of tolerance. AIC considers them suitable for people in clinical and serological remission who have also excluded oats for at least six months, starting under medical supervision.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"},{"titolo":"American College of Gastroenterology Guidelines Update: Diagnosis and Management of Celiac Disease (Rubio-Tapia A et al., Am J Gastroenterol 2023;118:59-76; PubMed 36602836); full text read from a publisher PDF copy","editore":"American College of Gastroenterology (ACG)","anno":2023,"url":"https://doi.org/10.14309/ajg.0000000000002075"},{"titolo":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD) guideline for coeliac disease and other gluten-related disorders (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2019;7(5):583-613; PMC6545713); full text read from a publisher PDF copy","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2019,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2050640619844125"},{"titolo":"I cereali permessi (includes the current AIC position on oats; page modified 2026-03-07)","editore":"AIC Associazione Italiana Celiachia","anno":2026,"url":"https://www.celiachia.it/dieta-senza-glutine/gestire-dieta-senza-glutine/i-cereali-permessi/"},{"titolo":"I cereali vietati (page modified 2026-03-12)","editore":"AIC Associazione Italiana Celiachia","anno":2026,"url":"https://www.celiachia.it/dieta-senza-glutine/gestire-dieta-senza-glutine/i-cereali-vietati/"},{"titolo":"Oats and the gluten free diet (accessed 2026-11-06; no publication date shown)","editore":"Coeliac UK","anno":null,"url":"https://www.coeliac.org.uk/living-with-coeliac-disease/food-and-drink/food-and-drink-information/oats/"},{"titolo":"Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) No 828/2014 on the requirements for the provision of information to consumers on the absence or reduced presence of gluten in food, Annex","editore":"EUR-Lex, European Union","anno":2014,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32014R0828"}]},{"id":"celiac_eu_labels","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"prefer","cibi":["packaged foods labelled 'senza glutine' / 'gluten-free' / 'glutenfrei'"],"it":"Etichette UE: 'senza glutine' solo se il glutine non supera 20 mg/kg; 'con contenuto di glutine molto basso' indica fino a 100 mg/kg e non equivale a 'senza glutine'. L'avena in un prodotto 'senza glutine' deve essere prodotta in modo da evitare contaminazioni e non superare 20 mg/kg.","en":"EU labels: 'gluten-free' only if gluten is no more than 20 mg/kg; 'very low gluten' means up to 100 mg/kg and is not the same as gluten-free. Oats in a gluten-free product must be produced to avoid contamination and contain no more than 20 mg/kg.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) No 828/2014 on the requirements for the provision of information to consumers on the absence or reduced presence of gluten in food, Annex","editore":"EUR-Lex, European Union","anno":2014,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32014R0828"},{"titolo":"Regolamento di esecuzione (UE) n. 828/2014 della Commissione, Allegato (testo italiano)","editore":"EUR-Lex, Unione europea","anno":2014,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/IT/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32014R0828"},{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"}]},{"id":"celiac_naturally_gf_grains","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"prefer","cibi":["rice (brown, basmati, black)","maize","buckwheat","quinoa","millet","sorghum","teff","amaranth"],"it":"Cereali e pseudocereali naturalmente senza glutine (riso, mais, grano saraceno, quinoa, miglio, sorgo, teff, amaranto) sono adatti, ma i prodotti a base di cereali possono essere contaminati: preferisci quelli con la dicitura 'senza glutine'.","en":"Naturally gluten-free grains and pseudo-cereals (rice, maize, buckwheat, quinoa, millet, sorghum, teff, amaranth) are suitable, but grain products can be contaminated: prefer those labelled gluten-free.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"},{"titolo":"I cereali permessi (includes the current AIC position on oats; page modified 2026-03-07)","editore":"AIC Associazione Italiana Celiachia","anno":2026,"url":"https://www.celiachia.it/dieta-senza-glutine/gestire-dieta-senza-glutine/i-cereali-permessi/"}]},{"id":"celiac_nutrient_deficiencies","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"monitor","cibi":["iron sources","calcium sources","folate sources","vitamin B12 sources"],"it":"Nella celiachia le carenze sono frequenti: ferro (dal 7% all'80% dei nuovi diagnosticati), vitamina D e altre vitamine liposolubili, calcio, B12, folati, zinco e rame; anche una dieta senza glutine sbilanciata può causarne. ESsCD raccomanda una valutazione nutrizionale e un dietista esperto in celiachia.","en":"Deficiencies are common in celiac disease: iron (7% to 80% of newly diagnosed patients), vitamin D and other fat-soluble vitamins, calcium, B12, folate, zinc and copper; a poorly balanced gluten-free diet can also cause them. ESsCD recommends a nutritional assessment and a dietitian experienced in celiac disease.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"},{"titolo":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD) guideline for coeliac disease and other gluten-related disorders (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2019;7(5):583-613; PMC6545713); full text read from a publisher PDF copy","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2019,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2050640619844125"}]},{"id":"celiac_followup_labs","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"monitor","cibi":[],"it":"Controlli suggeriti da ESsCD 2025 negli adulti: alla diagnosi emocromo, stato del ferro, folati, B12, funzione tiroidea, enzimi epatici, albumina, calcio, fosfato, vitamina D e glicemia; dopo 4 a 6 mesi ripetere gli esami alterati; a 12 mesi sierologia (anti-TG2 IgA); poi ogni 1 o 2 anni sierologia (facoltativa se già negativizzata) e funzione tiroidea.","en":"ESsCD 2025 suggested adult follow-up: at diagnosis full blood count, iron status, folate, B12, thyroid function, liver enzymes, albumin, calcium, phosphate, vitamin D and glucose; at 4 to 6 months repeat abnormal tests; at 12 months serology (IgA anti-TG2); then every 1 to 2 years serology (optional once negative) and thyroid function.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"}]},{"id":"celiac_ttg_interpretation","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"monitor","cibi":[],"it":"Anti-TG2 (tTG) IgA nel follow-up: un valore positivo durante la dieta senza glutine suggerisce esposizione al glutine o scarsa aderenza; un valore negativo non dimostra un'aderenza perfetta né la guarigione della mucosa. Di solito si normalizza entro circa 12 mesi.","en":"IgA anti-TG2 (tTG) in follow-up: a positive value on a gluten-free diet suggests gluten exposure or poor adherence; a negative value does not prove strict adherence or mucosal healing. It usually normalises within about 12 months.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"}]},{"id":"celiac_lactose","condizione":"celiac","tipo":"check_with_doctor","cibi":["milk","lactose-containing dairy"],"it":"Alla diagnosi, se persistono sintomi intestinali per carenza secondaria di lattasi, una restrizione temporanea del lattosio può aiutare (raccomandazione condizionale ESsCD 2025); la dieta deve comunque includere latticini o alternative fortificate.","en":"At diagnosis, if gut symptoms persist because of secondary lactase deficiency, temporary lactose restriction can help (conditional ESsCD 2025 recommendation); the diet should still include dairy or fortified alternatives.","evidenza":"guideline","fonti":[{"titolo":"ESsCD 2025 Updated Guidelines on the Diagnosis and Management of Coeliac Disease in Adults. Part 2: Management, Follow-up, and Complex Disease Courses (Al-Toma A et al., United European Gastroenterol J 2026;14(2):e70195); full text read from https://eprints.whiterose.ac.uk/id/eprint/239170/","editore":"European Society for the Study of Coeliac Disease (ESsCD)","anno":2026,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ueg2.70195"}]},{"id":"general_vitamin_c_iron","condizione":"general","tipo":"prefer","cibi":["lemon juice","vitamin C-rich fruit and vegetables"],"it":"Limone su verdure e legumi: la vitamina C (acido ascorbico) è il più efficace favorente dell'assorbimento del ferro non-eme; si degrada con la cottura, quindi meglio aggiungere il limone a crudo. In una dieta varia l'effetto è più modesto.","en":"Lemon on vegetables and legumes: vitamin C (ascorbic acid) is the most effective enhancer of non-haem iron absorption; it degrades with cooking, so add lemon raw. In a varied diet the effect is more modest.","evidenza":"expert-opinion","fonti":[{"titolo":"Enhancers of iron absorption: ascorbic acid and other organic acids (Teucher B et al., Int J Vitam Nutr Res 2004;74:403-419)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2004,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15743017/"},{"titolo":"Iron bioavailability and dietary reference values (Hurrell R, Egli I, Am J Clin Nutr 2010;91:1461S-1467S)","editore":"PubMed","anno":2010,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20200263/"}]},{"id":"general_mineral_water","condizione":"general","tipo":"prefer","cibi":["natural mineral water labelled 'calcica' / 'contains calcium'","natural mineral water labelled 'indicata per le diete povere di sodio'"],"it":"Acqua minerale: per legge UE la dicitura 'Calcica' (in tedesco 'Calciumhaltig') indica calcio superiore a 150 mg/l; 'Indicata per le diete povere di sodio' indica sodio inferiore a 20 mg/l, utile con il sale moderato; 'Sodica' indica sodio superiore a 200 mg/l.","en":"Mineral water: under EU law the indication 'Contains calcium' (Italian 'Calcica', German 'Calciumhaltig') means calcium above 150 mg/l; 'Suitable for a low-sodium diet' means sodium below 20 mg/l, useful with moderate salt; 'Contains sodium' means sodium above 200 mg/l.","evidenza":"regulation","fonti":[{"titolo":"Directive 2009/54/EC on the exploitation and marketing of natural mineral waters (Recast), Annex III","editore":"EUR-Lex, European Union","anno":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"},{"titolo":"Direttiva 2009/54/CE sull'utilizzazione e la commercializzazione delle acque minerali naturali (rifusione), Allegato III (testo italiano)","editore":"EUR-Lex, Unione europea","anno":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/IT/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"},{"titolo":"Richtlinie 2009/54/EG über die Gewinnung von und den Handel mit natürlichen Mineralwässern (Neufassung), Anhang III (deutscher Text)","editore":"EUR-Lex, Europäische Union","anno":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"}]}],"egfr":{"formula_text":"eGFRcr = 142 x min(Scr/kappa, 1)^alpha x max(Scr/kappa, 1)^-1.200 x 0.9938^Age x 1.012 [if female]. Scr = standardized serum creatinine in mg/dL (divide µmol/L by 88.4); Age in years; result in mL/min/1.73 m2. min(Scr/kappa, 1) is the smaller of Scr/kappa and 1; max(Scr/kappa, 1) is the larger. No race coefficient.","female":{"kappa":0.7,"alpha":-0.241,"factor":1.012},"male":{"kappa":0.9,"alpha":-0.302,"factor":1},"constant":142,"exp_above":-1.2,"age_base":0.9938,"sources":[{"title":"New Creatinine- and Cystatin C-Based Equations to Estimate GFR without Race (Inker LA et al., N Engl J Med 2021;385:1737-1749), Table 2","publisher":"New England Journal of Medicine (PMC author manuscript)","year":2021,"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8822996/"},{"title":"CKD-EPI Creatinine Equation (2021)","publisher":"National Kidney Foundation","year":2021,"url":"https://www.kidney.org/professionals/ckd-epi-creatinine-equation-2021"},{"title":"KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of Chronic Kidney Disease (Kidney Int 2024;105(4S):S117-S314)","publisher":"KDIGO","year":2024,"url":"https://kdigo.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/KDIGO-2024-CKD-Guideline.pdf"}],"verified":true,"verification_note":"Coefficients read in Inker 2021 Table 2 (2021 CKD-EPI creatinine, eGFRcr(AS): intercept 142, a1 F -0.241 / M -0.302, a2 -1.200, age 0.9938, female 1.012; kappa 0.7 F / 0.9 M) and identical on the NKF page. KDIGO 2024 CKD Recommendation 1.2.4.1 (validated equation), Practice Point 1.2.4.1 (same equation within a region) and 1.2.4.2 (avoid race).","test_vectors_computed":[{"sex":"female","age":30,"scr_mg_dl":0.7,"egfr":119.2},{"sex":"female","age":30,"scr_mg_dl":0.9,"egfr":88.2},{"sex":"female","age":30,"scr_mg_dl":1.2,"egfr":62.5},{"sex":"male","age":50,"scr_mg_dl":1.3,"egfr":66.9}],"test_vectors_note":"Computed in this session from the verified formula for unit tests; these numbers are not printed in the sources.","app_rules":"Prefer the eGFR printed on the report and store its equation name; compute CKD-EPI 2021 only when the report has creatinine but no eGFR, and label it as app-calculated. European labs may report EKFC or CKD-EPI 2009 (KDIGO 2024 discusses EKFC); do not mix equations in one trend."},"bmi":{"categories":[{"min":0,"max":18.5,"label_en":"Underweight","label_it":"Sottopeso"},{"min":18.5,"max":25,"label_en":"Normal range","label_it":"Normopeso"},{"min":25,"max":30,"label_en":"Pre-obese (overweight)","label_it":"Sovrappeso (pre-obesità)"},{"min":30,"max":35,"label_en":"Obese class I","label_it":"Obesità di classe I"},{"min":35,"max":40,"label_en":"Obese class II","label_it":"Obesità di classe II"},{"min":40,"max":null,"label_en":"Obese class III","label_it":"Obesità di classe III"}],"boundary_rule":"min inclusive, max exclusive; max null means no upper bound. WHO TRS 894 Table 2.1 prints: underweight <18.50; normal range 18.50 to 24.99; overweight >=25.00 (pre-obese 25.00 to 29.99); obese class I 30.00 to 34.99; class II 35.00 to 39.99; class III >=40.00.","formula":"BMI = weight (kg) / height (m)^2","notes":"WHO: cut-offs are age-independent and the same for both sexes; BMI may not reflect the same fatness in all populations and fat distribution (waist circumference) also matters. The WHO fact sheet confirms overweight >=25 and obesity >=30 for adults. Italian labels sottopeso, normopeso, sovrappeso and obesità are verified on ISS EpiCentro; the Italian class I to III wording is a translation, not checked against an Italian source.","sources":[{"title":"Obesity: preventing and managing the global epidemic. Report of a WHO Consultation (WHO Technical Report Series 894), Table 2.1","publisher":"World Health Organization","year":2000,"url":"https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/42330"},{"title":"Obesity and overweight, fact sheet","publisher":"World Health Organization","year":null,"url":"https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/obesity-and-overweight"},{"title":"Obesità (EpiCentro), classi di peso per gli adulti indicate dal BMI","publisher":"Istituto Superiore di Sanità (ISS)","year":null,"url":"https://www.epicentro.iss.it/obesita/"}],"verified":true},"acqua":{"threshold_mg_per_l":150,"comparison":"greater_than","label_it":"Calcica","label_en":"Contains calcium","label_de":"Calciumhaltig","criterion_text_en":"Calcium content greater than 150 mg/l","criterion_text_it":"Il tenore di calcio è superiore a 150 mg/l","criterion_text_de":"Der Calciumgehalt beträgt mehr als 150 mg/l","related_indications":[{"label_en":"Suitable for a low-sodium diet","label_it":"Indicata per le diete povere di sodio","label_de":"Geeignet für natriumarme Ernährung","criterion":"sodium less than 20 mg/l"},{"label_en":"Contains sodium","label_it":"Sodica","label_de":"Natriumhaltig","criterion":"sodium greater than 200 mg/l"},{"label_en":"Contains magnesium","label_it":"Magnesiaca","label_de":"Magnesiumhaltig","criterion":"magnesium greater than 50 mg/l"}],"correction_to_brief":"The brief said 'at least 150 mg/l' and 'contenente calcio'. EUR-Lex Annex III says 'greater than 150 mg/l' (IT 'superiore a 150 mg/l', DE 'mehr als 150 mg/l') and the Italian indication is 'Calcica'. A water with exactly 150 mg/l does not qualify.","legal_status_note":"EUR-Lex lists only the original consolidated version (16/07/2009) for this Directive, so Annex III is unchanged as published.","sources":[{"title":"Directive 2009/54/EC on the exploitation and marketing of natural mineral waters (Recast), Annex III","publisher":"EUR-Lex, European Union","year":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"},{"title":"Direttiva 2009/54/CE sull'utilizzazione e la commercializzazione delle acque minerali naturali (rifusione), Allegato III (testo italiano)","publisher":"EUR-Lex, Unione europea","year":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/IT/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"},{"title":"Richtlinie 2009/54/EG über die Gewinnung von und den Handel mit natürlichen Mineralwässern (Neufassung), Anhang III (deutscher Text)","publisher":"EUR-Lex, Europäische Union","year":2009,"url":"https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32009L0054"}],"verified":true},"variabilita":{"usabile":false,"nota":"biologicalvariation.eu was reachable, but its copyright statement (site footer and /disclaimer page) says: 'Systematic extraction, reproduction or redistribution of database content, incorporation of the content into another database, software application, digital product or service, or commercial use requires prior written permission from EFLM and a written agreement with EFLM and will be subject to a fee.' Therefore no CVI or analytical performance specification was extracted or included. Permission requests go to the EFLM Office named on the site.","rcv":{"text":"RCV (%) = sqrt(2) x Z x sqrt(CVA^2 + CVI^2), with CVA = analytical CV of the lab method and CVI = within-subject biological CV, both in %. Z = 1.96 for a bidirectional change at the 5% significance level. Log-normal (asymmetric) RCV variants exist; their exact formula was not verified here.","sources":[{"title":"Reference change values (Fraser CG, Clin Chem Lab Med 2011;50:807-812)","publisher":"PubMed","year":2011,"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21958344/"},{"title":"Biological variation and reference change value of the estimated glomerular filtration rate in humans: a systematic review and meta-analysis (Thöni S et al., Front Med 2022;9:1009358)","publisher":"PubMed Central","year":2022,"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9583397/"}]},"alternative":null},"domande":["Which drugs does Sofia take now (hydroxychloroquine, mycophenolate, azathioprine, tacrolimus, voclosporin, cyclosporine, prednisone, ACE inhibitor or ARB, anticoagulant or aspirin)? Drug-food points carry an applies_if field and must be switched on per medication.","Is she considered immunosuppressed? This switches on the FDA raw-sprout rule and any wider raw-food safety rules the doctor wants.","Oats: AIC (live page, modified 2026-03) asks for clinical and serological remission, at least six months of oat-free diet and medical supervision; ESsCD 2025 and ACG 2023 allow certified gluten-free oats from diagnosis with tolerance monitoring. Which position does her gastroenterologist follow?","Protein: KDIGO 2021 expresses 0.8 to 1.0 g/kg/day per ideal body weight. Is the nutritionist's 1 g/kg per actual or ideal weight?","Garlic: only patient-organisation advice with mechanistic reasoning. Does her rheumatologist want culinary garlic limited? The app should not label garlic as dangerous.","Omega-3 supplement: dose, product and any anticoagulant, antiplatelet or NSAID use need the doctor's approval before the app shows it as active.","Vitamin D: target and dose are for her doctor; disease-activity benefit is uncertain.","EFLM biological variation data: request written permission from EFLM, or ship the app without CVI-based RCV (or let the lab provide CVA and CVI).","Analytical CV (CVA) for RCV must come from her laboratory; it is method specific.","Folate (ng/mL vs nmol/L) and vitamin B12 (pg/mL vs pmol/L) conversion factors were not verified from an authoritative source: trend within one unit only.","Urea / BUN ('Azotemia', 'Harnstoff', 'Harnstoff-N') was left out on purpose: urea and urea nitrogen units differ and no authoritative conversion was verified. Treat as a custom marker without conversion if she wants it.","tTG-IgA and anti-dsDNA are kit specific; store value divided by the report's upper limit of normal for cross-lab comparison.","Alias collision: Italian 'PCR' = C-reactive protein (blood) while KDIGO 'PCR' = urine protein-creatinine ratio. Disambiguate by specimen and unit.","Albumin depends on method (bromocresol green vs bromocresol purple or immunoassay); store the method if printed.","Which eGFR equation does each of her labs print (CKD-EPI 2009, CKD-EPI 2021, EKFC)?","Aliases were compiled from common Italian, Austrian and German report wording and are not individually sourced; validate them against her real reports.","Not verified (full text not retrieved): ACR 2022 glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis guideline (abstract only), EULAR 2022 cardiovascular risk and 2021 lifestyle recommendations (paywalled), NIH ODS fact sheets (HTTP 403). Equivalent points were sourced from KDIGO, EULAR 2010/2023 and peer-reviewed papers instead.","Plan items outside this brief were not reviewed: 3 coffees/day, 2 to 3 L water/day, tuna and swordfish limits (mercury)."]};
